{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "def is_not_prime(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies if an integer is a non-prime number.\n    Returns True for non-primes, False for primes or numbers less than or equal to 1.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 1:\n        return False\n    if number == 2:\n        return False\n\n    # Check for divisibility from 2 up to the square root of the number.\n    for i in range(2, int(number**0.5) + 1):\n        if number % i == 0:\n            return True  # Found a factor, so it's a non-prime number.\n\n    return False  # No factors found, so it's a prime number."}
