{"task_id": "Mbpp/3", "solution": "import math\ndef is_not_prime(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given integer is a non-prime number.\n    Returns True for non-prime numbers, False for prime numbers.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number <= 1:\n        return True  # Numbers less than or equal to 1 are non-prime by definition.\n    if number == 2:\n        return False  # 2 is the only even prime number.\n    if number % 2 == 0:\n        return True  # Even numbers greater than 2 are non-prime.\n\n    # Check for odd divisors from 3 up to the square root of the number.\n    for i in range(3, int(math.sqrt(number)) + 1, 2):\n        if number % i == 0:\n            return True  # Found a divisor, so it's a non-prime number.\n\n    return False  # No divisors found, so it's a prime number."}
