{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "_memo = [0, 1, 1]\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth Newman-Conway number P(n) using memoization.\n    It dynamically grows an internal cache to store computed values.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Ensure _memo is large enough to store P(n) and initialize if needed.\n    while len(_memo) <= n:\n        _memo.append(0)\n\n    # Return cached value if already computed.\n    if _memo[n] != 0:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    # Calculate P(n) using the recursive formula P(P(n-1)) + P(n - P(n-1)).\n    # Store P(n-1) once to avoid recomputing it for both terms.\n    p_n_minus_1 = sequence(n - 1)\n    val = sequence(p_n_minus_1) + sequence(n - p_n_minus_1)\n    _memo[n] = val\n    return val"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/84", "solution": "_memo = {}\ndef sequence(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the nth number of the Newman-Conway sequence.\n    Uses memoization to store previously computed values.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    if n == 1:\n        result = 1\n    elif n == 2:\n        result = 1\n    else:\n        p_n_minus_1 = sequence(n - 1)\n        result = sequence(p_n_minus_1) + sequence(n - p_n_minus_1)\n\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
