{"task_id": "Mbpp/92", "solution": "def is_undulating(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a given integer is 'undulating', meaning its digits strictly alternate.\n    Single-digit numbers are undulating; numbers with identical adjacent digits are not.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_number = str(number)\n    digits = [int(d) for d in s_number]\n\n    if len(digits) == 1:\n        return True\n\n    for i in range(len(digits) - 1):\n        # Check for adjacent identical digits (e.g., 11, 122).\n        if digits[i] == digits[i+1]:\n            return False\n\n        # Check for the alternating pattern (e.g., 123 is not undulating as 1 != 3).\n        if i + 2 < len(digits):\n            if digits[i] != digits[i+2]:\n                return False\n\n    return True"}
