{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Eulerian number A(n, m) using dynamic programming.\n    Assumes n and m are non-negative integers as per critical requirements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0 and m == 0:\n        return 1\n    if m >= n:\n        return 0\n\n    # Initialize a DP table for A(i, j).\n    # The table size is (n+1) x (n+1) to accommodate up to A(n, n) indices.\n    dp = [[0] * (n + 1) for _ in range(n + 1)]\n\n    # Base case: A(0, 0) = 1\n    dp[0][0] = 1\n\n    # Fill the DP table using the recurrence relation:\n    # A(i, j) = (j + 1) * A(i - 1, j) + (i - j) * A(i - 1, j - 1)\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        for j in range(0, i):  # A(i, j) is 0 if j >= i, so we only compute for j < i\n            term1 = (j + 1) * dp[i - 1][j]\n            term2 = 0\n            if j - 1 >= 0:  # Handle the case where j-1 is out of bounds for dp[i-1]\n                term2 = (i - j) * dp[i - 1][j - 1]\n            dp[i][j] = term1 + term2\n\n    return dp[n][m]"}
