{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "from typing import List, Set, Any\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists: List[List[Any]]) -> Set[Any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the intersection of all sub-lists within a given nested list to find common elements.\n    Returns a set containing elements present in every sub-list of the input.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    common_set = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    for sub_list in nested_lists[1:]:\n        current_set = set(sub_list)\n        common_set = common_set.intersection(current_set)\n        if not common_set:  # Optimization: if common_set is empty, no further intersections will add elements\n            break\n\n    return common_set"}
