{"task_id": "Mbpp/111", "solution": "from typing import List, Any, Set\ndef common_in_nested_lists(nested_lists: List[List[Any]]) -> Set[Any]:\n    \"\"\"Finds common elements across all sub-lists in a nested list.\n    It returns an empty set if the input list is empty or the first sub-list is empty.\"\"\"\n    if not nested_lists:\n        return set()\n\n    # Initialize common_elements with the set of the first sub-list.\n    common_elements = set(nested_lists[0])\n\n    # Iterate through the remaining sub-lists, performing intersection.\n    for sublist in nested_lists[1:]:\n        common_elements.intersection_update(sublist)\n        if not common_elements:\n            break  # Early termination if no common elements remain.\n\n    return common_elements"}
