{"task_id": "Mbpp/119", "solution": "def search(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the element that appears only once in a sorted array.\n    Assumes all other elements appear an even number of times.\n    \"\"\"\n    n = len(arr)\n    # Iterate through the array in steps of 2.\n    for i in range(0, n - 1, 2):\n        # If the current element is not equal to the next, it's the unique one.\n        if arr[i] != arr[i+1]:\n            return arr[i]\n    # If the loop completes, the last element is the unique one.\n    return arr[n-1]"}
