{"task_id": "Mbpp/119", "solution": "def search(arr: list[int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the single unique element in a sorted array where all other elements appear twice.\n    Uses a binary search approach to achieve O(log n) time complexity.\n    \"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(arr) - 1\n\n    while low < high:\n        mid = (low + high) // 2\n\n        # Ensure mid always points to an even index for pair comparison.\n        # If mid is odd, decrement it to make it the start of a potential pair.\n        if mid % 2 == 1:\n            mid -= 1\n\n        # If arr[mid] and arr[mid+1] are equal, the unique element is to the right.\n        # Advance low past this pair.\n        if arr[mid] == arr[mid+1]:\n            low = mid + 2\n        # If arr[mid] and arr[mid+1] are different, the unique element is at or before mid.\n        # Narrow the search space to [low, mid].\n        else:\n            high = mid\n\n    # When the loop terminates, low (which equals high) is the index of the unique element.\n    return arr[low]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/103", "solution": "def eulerian_num(n: int, m: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the Eulerian number a(n, m).\n    It implements the sum formula: sum_{k=0 to m} (-1)^k * C(n+1, k) * (m - k + 1)^n.\n    \"\"\"\n\n    def _factorial(val: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Computes the factorial of a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n        res = 1\n        for i in range(1, val + 1):\n            res *= i\n        return res\n\n    def _combinations(N: int, K: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"Calculates the binomial coefficient C(N, K).\"\"\"\n        if K < 0 or K > N:\n            return 0\n        return _factorial(N) // (_factorial(K) * _factorial(N - K))\n\n    eulerian_sum = 0\n    for k in range(m + 1):\n        term = ((-1)**k) * _combinations(n + 1, k) * ((m - k + 1)**n)\n        eulerian_sum += term\n\n    return eulerian_sum"}
