{"task_id": "Mbpp/109", "solution": "def odd_Equivalent(binary_string: str, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the count of odd numbers derived from rotating a given binary string\n    a specified number of times.\n    \"\"\"\n    _validate_binary_string(binary_string)\n    _validate_rotation_count(n)\n\n    odd_count = 0\n    current_binary_string = binary_string\n\n    for _ in range(n):\n        decimal_equivalent = _binary_to_decimal(current_binary_string)\n        if _is_odd(decimal_equivalent):\n            odd_count += 1\n        current_binary_string = _rotate_string_left(current_binary_string)\n\n    return odd_count\ndef _rotate_string_left(s: str) -> str:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs a single left cyclic rotation on the input string s.\n    Assumes 's' is a non-empty string.\n    \"\"\"\n    return s[1:] + s[0]\ndef _binary_to_decimal(binary_str: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a binary string binary_str to its decimal integer equivalent.\n    Assumes 'binary_str' is a valid, non-empty binary string.\n    \"\"\"\n    return int(binary_str, 2)\ndef _is_odd(number: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Checks if an integer number is odd.\n    \"\"\"\n    return number % 2 != 0"}
