{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(integer_array: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the ratio of zero elements to non-zero elements in an array.\n    Returns float('inf') if there are no non-zero elements.\"\"\"\n    zero_elements = 0\n    non_zero_elements = 0\n\n    for element in integer_array:\n        if element == 0:\n            zero_elements += 1\n        else:\n            non_zero_elements += 1\n\n    if non_zero_elements > 0:\n        ratio = float(zero_elements) / non_zero_elements\n    else:\n        ratio = float('inf')\n\n    return ratio"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/137", "solution": "def zero_count(data: list[int]) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the ratio of zero elements to non-zero elements in an array.\n    Returns 0.0 if there are no non-zero elements to avoid division by zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    zero_count_val = 0\n    non_zero_count_val = 0\n\n    for element in data:\n        if element == 0:\n            zero_count_val += 1\n        else:\n            non_zero_count_val += 1\n\n    if non_zero_count_val == 0:\n        return 0.0\n    else:\n        return float(zero_count_val) / non_zero_count_val"}
