{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets all even-indexed bits of the input number to 1.\n    The mask covers all even bits up to the most significant bit of the input number.\"\"\"\n\n    # Determine the number of bits to consider for the mask.\n    # We take the maximum of 1 (to ensure bit 0 is always considered) and the number's actual bit length.\n    num_bits = max(1, number.bit_length())\n\n    # Create a mask with all even-indexed bits set to 1 within the determined length.\n    mask = 0\n    for i in range(0, num_bits, 2):\n        mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    # Perform a bitwise OR operation to set the even bits of the input number.\n    return number | mask"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/237", "solution": "from typing import List, Tuple, Any, Dict\ndef check_occurences(list_of_tuples: List[Tuple[Any, ...]]) -> Dict[Tuple[Any, ...], int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Counts occurrences of canonical tuple forms in a list of tuples.\n    It sorts elements within each tuple to create a canonical representation.\n    \"\"\"\n    occurrence_counts: Dict[Tuple[Any, ...], int] = {}\n\n    for original_tuple in list_of_tuples:\n        # Convert to list, sort, and convert back to tuple for canonical form.\n        list_representation = list(original_tuple)\n        list_representation.sort()\n        canonical_tuple = tuple(list_representation)\n\n        # Increment count for the canonical tuple.\n        if canonical_tuple in occurrence_counts:\n            occurrence_counts[canonical_tuple] += 1\n        else:\n            occurrence_counts[canonical_tuple] = 1\n\n    return occurrence_counts"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/235", "solution": "def even_bit_set_number(number: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Sets all bits at odd positions (1, 3, 5, ...) within the number's effective length to 1.\n    This implementation ensures even_bit_set_number(10) == 10, as specified.\"\"\"\n\n    # Determine the effective bit length of the number.\n    effective_length = number.bit_length()\n\n    mask = 0\n    # Iterate through bit positions from 0 up to effective_length - 1.\n    # Only set bits at odd positions (1, 3, 5, ...).\n    for i in range(effective_length):\n        if i % 2 == 1:  # Check if the bit position is odd (e.g., 1, 3, 5)\n            mask |= (1 << i)\n\n    # Apply the mask: perform a bitwise OR to set the specified bits.\n    return number | mask"}
