{"task_id": "Mbpp/239", "solution": "def get_total_number_of_sequences(m: int, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the total number of valid sequences of length n.\n    Each element must be positive, >= twice the previous, and <= m.\n    \"\"\"\n    memo = {} # Stores results of subproblems for memoization.\n\n    def count_sequences_recursive(current_length: int, prev_element_value: int, m_constraint: int, n_constraint: int) -> int:\n        \"\"\"\n        Recursively counts sequences, utilizing memoization.\n        n_constraint is present as per design, but not used in logic as current_length suffices.\n        \"\"\"\n        state_key = (current_length, prev_element_value)\n        if state_key in memo:\n            return memo[state_key]\n\n        if current_length == 0:\n            return 1  # Base case: A valid sequence segment of the desired length has been formed.\n\n        current_sequences_count = 0\n        start_next_element = 2 * prev_element_value\n        for next_element_candidate in range(start_next_element, m_constraint + 1):\n            current_sequences_count += count_sequences_recursive(\n                current_length - 1,\n                next_element_candidate,\n                m_constraint,\n                n_constraint\n            )\n\n        memo[state_key] = current_sequences_count\n        return current_sequences_count\n\n    total_number_of_sequences = 0\n    # Iterate through all possible values for the first element of the sequence.\n    # A first element must be positive and less than or equal to m.\n    for first_element in range(1, m + 1):\n        # We need to find sequences of length (n-1) after placing the first element.\n        total_number_of_sequences += count_sequences_recursive(n - 1, first_element, m, n)\n\n    return total_number_of_sequences"}
