{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def count_Primes_nums(n):\n    \"\"\"Calculates the number of prime numbers strictly less than n.\n    This function assumes n is a non-negative integer.\"\"\"\n\n    def is_prime(num):\n        \"\"\"Checks if a number is prime using trial division.\"\"\"\n        if num < 2:\n            return False\n        if num == 2:\n            return True\n        if num % 2 == 0:\n            return False\n        i = 3\n        while i * i <= num:\n            if num % i == 0:\n                return False\n            i += 2\n        return True\n\n    count = 0\n    for number in range(2, n):\n        if is_prime(number):\n            count += 1\n    return count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/256", "solution": "def _is_prime(num: int) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if a number is prime. Helper for prime counting.\"\"\"\n    if num < 2:\n        return False\n    if num == 2:\n        return True\n    if num % 2 == 0:\n        return False\n    # Check for odd divisors up to the square root of num\n    i = 3\n    while i * i <= num:\n        if num % i == 0:\n            return False\n        i += 2\n    return True\ndef count_Primes_nums(limit: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts prime numbers strictly less than the given limit.\"\"\"\n    prime_count = 0\n    # Iterate through numbers from 2 up to, but not including, the limit\n    for num in range(2, limit):\n        if _is_prime(num):\n            prime_count += 1\n    return prime_count"}
