{"task_id": "Mbpp/264", "solution": "def dog_age(human_years: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates a dog's age in dog years based on human years.\n    Applies specific conversion factors and rounds the result to the nearest integer (round half up).\n    \"\"\"\n    if human_years < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Human years cannot be negative.\")\n\n    first_two_years_factor = 10.5\n    subsequent_years_factor = 4\n\n    dog_years_float = 0.0\n\n    if human_years == 0:\n        dog_years_float = 0.0\n    elif human_years <= 2:\n        dog_years_float = human_years * first_two_years_factor\n    else:\n        dog_years_float = (2 * first_two_years_factor) + ((human_years - 2) * subsequent_years_factor)\n\n    # Round to the nearest integer, applying round half up for positive values.\n    return int(dog_years_float + 0.5)"}
