{"task_id": "Mbpp/264", "solution": "def dog_age(human_years: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates a dog's age in dog years based on human years, with input validation and specific rounding.\n    Raises TypeError if input is not an integer or ValueError if input is negative.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not isinstance(human_years, int):\n        raise TypeError(\"human_years must be an integer.\")\n    if human_years < 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"human_years cannot be negative.\")\n\n    calculated_dog_years = 0.0\n\n    if human_years <= 2:\n        calculated_dog_years = human_years * 10.5\n    else:\n        # First two years are 10.5 dog years each\n        calculated_dog_years = (2 * 10.5)\n        # Subsequent years are 4 dog years each\n        calculated_dog_years += (human_years - 2) * 4\n\n    # Round to the nearest integer, with halves rounded up (e.g., 2.5 rounds to 3).\n    return int(calculated_dog_years + 0.5)"}
