{"task_id": "Mbpp/308", "solution": "import heapq\ndef large_product(list1, list2, n):\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the n largest products from two lists, picking one factor from each.\n    Uses a max-heap (simulated with a min-heap) to efficiently extract products.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0 or not list1 or not list2:\n        return []\n\n    list1.sort()\n    list2.sort()\n\n    result = []\n    heap = []  # Stores (-product, index1, index2) to simulate a max-heap\n    visited = set()  # Stores (index1, index2) pairs to prevent duplicate processing\n\n    # Start with the product of the largest elements from both lists\n    i = len(list1) - 1\n    j = len(list2) - 1\n\n    heapq.heappush(heap, (-list1[i] * list2[j], i, j))\n    visited.add((i, j))\n\n    while len(result) < n and heap:\n        neg_prod, cur_i, cur_j = heapq.heappop(heap)\n        result.append(-neg_prod)\n\n        # Explore the product formed by decrementing the first list's index\n        if cur_i > 0 and (cur_i - 1, cur_j) not in visited:\n            new_prod = list1[cur_i - 1] * list2[cur_j]\n            heapq.heappush(heap, (-new_prod, cur_i - 1, cur_j))\n            visited.add((cur_i - 1, cur_j))\n\n        # Explore the product formed by decrementing the second list's index\n        if cur_j > 0 and (cur_i, cur_j - 1) not in visited:\n            new_prod = list1[cur_i] * list2[cur_j - 1]\n            heapq.heappush(heap, (-new_prod, cur_i, cur_j - 1))\n            visited.add((cur_i, cur_j - 1))\n\n    return result"}
