{"task_id": "Mbpp/312", "solution": "import math\ndef volume_cone(radius: float, height: float) -> float:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the volume of a cone given its radius and height.\n    The volume is calculated using the formula (1/3) * PI * radius^2 * height.\n\n    Args:\n        radius (float): The radius of the cone.\n        height (float): The height of the cone.\n\n    Returns:\n        float: The calculated volume of the cone.\n    \"\"\"\n    if radius <= 0 or height <= 0:\n        raise ValueError(\"Radius and height must be positive numbers.\")\n    return (1/3) * math.pi * (radius ** 2) * height"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/388", "solution": "def highest_Power_of_2(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the highest power of 2 that is less than or equal to n.\n    Returns 1 for n <= 0, as 2^0 is the smallest positive power of 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 1 # 2^0 is 1, the smallest positive power of 2.\n\n    # Start with p = 1. Keep multiplying by 2 until p * 2 > n.\n    p = 1\n    while (p << 1) <= n:\n        p <<= 1\n    return p"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n'th Lucas number.\n    Uses an iterative approach based on L(0)=2, L(1)=1, and L(k)=L(k-1)+L(k-2) for k > 1.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    elif n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize variables for L(0) and L(1)\n    a, b = 2, 1\n\n    # Iterate from L(2) up to L(n)\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        next_lucas = a + b\n        a = b\n        b = next_lucas\n\n    return b"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/389", "solution": "def find_lucas(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the n'th Lucas number. The sequence starts L(0)=2, L(1)=1, and L(n)=L(n-1)+L(n-2) for n>1.\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 2\n    if n == 1:\n        return 1\n\n    a, b = 2, 1\n    for _ in range(2, n + 1):\n        a, b = b, a + b\n    return b"}
