{"task_id": "Mbpp/392", "solution": "_memo: dict[int, int] = {}\ndef get_max_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the maximum sum based on f(n) = max( (f(n/2) + f(n/3) + f(n/4) + f(n/5)), n).\n    Uses memoization to optimize performance.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n <= 0:\n        return 0\n\n    if n in _memo:\n        return _memo[n]\n\n    sum_of_subproblems = (\n        get_max_sum(n // 2) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 3) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 4) +\n        get_max_sum(n // 5)\n    )\n\n    result = max(sum_of_subproblems, n)\n    _memo[n] = result\n    return result"}
