{"task_id": "Mbpp/305", "solution": "import re\ndef start_withp(input_strings: list[str]) -> tuple[str | None, str | None]:\n    \"\"\"Finds the first two words across input strings that start with 'p' (case-insensitive).\n    Returns them as a tuple; missing elements are None if fewer than two are found.\"\"\"\n    p_words = []\n    for s in input_strings:\n        # Extract words in their original casing\n        words = re.findall(r'\\b[a-zA-Z]+\\b', s)\n        for word in words:\n            # Check if the word, when lowercased, starts with 'p'\n            if word.lower().startswith('p'):\n                p_words.append(word) # Append the word in its original casing\n                if len(p_words) == 2:\n                    return (p_words[0], p_words[1])\n\n    # If fewer than two words are found, pad with None as per design\n    return (p_words[0] if len(p_words) > 0 else None, p_words[1] if len(p_words) > 1 else None)"}
