{"task_id": "Mbpp/440", "solution": "import re\nimport string\ndef find_adverb_position(sentence: str):\n    \"\"\"\n    Identifies the first word ending in \"ly\" (after punctuation removal) and returns its position and value.\n    Returns (start_index, end_index, cleaned_adverb) or None if no adverb is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    punctuation_chars = string.punctuation\n\n    # Use re.finditer to get all non-whitespace sequences and their spans\n    for match in re.finditer(r'\\S+', sentence):\n        original_word = match.group(0)\n        word_span_start = match.start()\n        word_span_end = match.end()\n\n        # Clean the word by stripping leading and trailing punctuation\n        cleaned_word = original_word.strip(punctuation_chars)\n\n        # Check if the cleaned word is not empty and ends with \"ly\"\n        if cleaned_word and cleaned_word.endswith(\"ly\"):\n            # Find the exact start index of the cleaned adverb within its original word's span\n            adverb_start_index = sentence.find(cleaned_word, word_span_start, word_span_end)\n            adverb_end_index = adverb_start_index + len(cleaned_word)\n            return (adverb_start_index, adverb_end_index, cleaned_word)\n\n    # If the loop completes, no adverb was found\n    return None"}
