{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def _get_perrin_sequence(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates the Perrin sequence up to the n-th term (inclusive).\n    P(0)=3, P(1)=0, P(2)=2, and P(k) = P(k-2) + P(k-3) for k > 2.\n    \"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return [3]\n    elif n == 1:\n        return [3, 0]\n    elif n == 2:\n        return [3, 0, 2]\n\n    perrin_seq = [3, 0, 2]\n    for i in range(3, n + 1):\n        next_perrin = perrin_seq[i - 2] + perrin_seq[i - 3]\n        perrin_seq.append(next_perrin)\n    return perrin_seq\ndef cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers up to the n-th term (inclusive, 0-indexed).\n    This function leverages an internal helper to generate the sequence.\n    \"\"\"\n    perrin_sequence = _get_perrin_sequence(n)\n    return sum(perrin_sequence)"}
