{"task_id": "Mbpp/448", "solution": "def cal_sum(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the sum of Perrin numbers from P(0) to P(n).\n    This function computes the sum using an iterative approach for the sequence.\"\"\"\n\n    # Base cases for Perrin numbers\n    p_0 = 3  # P(0)\n    p_1 = 0  # P(1)\n    p_2 = 2  # P(2)\n\n    # Handle small n values directly\n    if n == 0:\n        return p_0\n    if n == 1:\n        return p_0 + p_1\n    if n == 2:\n        return p_0 + p_1 + p_2\n\n    # Initialize sum with base cases and previous Perrin numbers for iteration\n    current_sum = p_0 + p_1 + p_2\n\n    # Store P(i-3), P(i-2), P(i-1) respectively\n    p_minus_3, p_minus_2, p_minus_1 = p_0, p_1, p_2\n\n    # Iterate from P(3) up to P(n)\n    for _ in range(3, n + 1):\n        # Calculate P(i) = P(i-2) + P(i-3)\n        p_current = p_minus_2 + p_minus_3\n        current_sum += p_current\n\n        # Update values for the next iteration\n        p_minus_3 = p_minus_2\n        p_minus_2 = p_minus_1\n        p_minus_1 = p_current\n\n    return current_sum"}
