{"task_id": "Mbpp/463", "solution": "def max_subarray_product(array: list[float | int]) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Computes the maximum product of a contiguous subarray within the given array.\n    Handles various input scenarios including positive, negative, and zero values.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return 0\n\n    max_product_ending_here = array[0]\n    min_product_ending_here = array[0]\n    overall_max_product = array[0]\n\n    for current_num in array[1:]:\n        # Store max_product_ending_here before it's updated, as min_product_ending_here\n        # also needs the old value of max_product_ending_here for its calculation.\n        temp_max_so_far = max_product_ending_here\n\n        max_product_ending_here = max(current_num,\n                                      temp_max_so_far * current_num,\n                                      min_product_ending_here * current_num)\n\n        min_product_ending_here = min(current_num,\n                                      temp_max_so_far * current_num,\n                                      min_product_ending_here * current_num)\n\n        overall_max_product = max(overall_max_product, max_product_ending_here)\n\n    return int(overall_max_product)"}
