{"task_id": "Mbpp/558", "solution": "def digit_distance_nums(num1, num2):\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the sum of absolute differences between corresponding digits of two integers.\n    Shorter numbers are conceptually padded with leading zeros to match the length of the longer number.\n    \"\"\"\n    s_num1 = str(num1)\n    s_num2 = str(num2)\n\n    max_length = max(len(s_num1), len(s_num2))\n\n    padded_s_num1 = s_num1.zfill(max_length)\n    padded_s_num2 = s_num2.zfill(max_length)\n\n    total_distance = 0\n    for i in range(max_length):\n        digit1 = int(padded_s_num1[i])\n        digit2 = int(padded_s_num2[i])\n        total_distance += abs(digit1 - digit2)\n\n    return total_distance"}
