{"task_id": "Mbpp/576", "solution": "def is_Sub_Array(list1: list, list2: list) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if list2 is a contiguous sublist of list1.\n    Returns True if found, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not list2:\n        return True\n\n    len1 = len(list1)\n    len2 = len(list2)\n\n    if len2 > len1:\n        return False\n\n    for i in range(len1 - len2 + 1):\n        if list1[i:i + len2] == list2:\n            return True\n\n    return False"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/586", "solution": "def split_Arr(input_list: list, n: int) -> list:\n    \"\"\"Splits a list at the nth element and appends the first part to the end.\n\n    Args:\n        input_list: The list to be split and reordered.\n        n: The integer index at which to split the list (0 <= n <= len(input_list)).\n\n    Returns:\n        A new list with the reordered elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    first_part = input_list[:n]\n    second_part = input_list[n:]\n    return second_part + first_part"}
