{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates and returns a sorted list of Ludic numbers up to a specified integer n.\n    It implements a sieve-like process where after identifying a Ludic number k,\n    every k-th number is removed from the remaining sequence of candidates.\n    \"\"\"\n    ludic_numbers = []\n    # Initialize the sequence of natural numbers from 1 up to n.\n    current_sequence = list(range(1, n + 1))\n\n    # The number 1 is always the first Ludic number.\n    if n >= 1:\n        ludic_numbers.append(1)\n        # Remove 1 from the sequence to start the sieving process from the next number.\n        current_sequence.remove(1)\n\n    # Continue the sieve process as long as there are candidate numbers.\n    while current_sequence:\n        # The first element in the current_sequence is the next Ludic number.\n        k = current_sequence.pop(0)\n        # If the candidate exceeds n, no further Ludic numbers can be found.\n        if k > n:\n            break\n        ludic_numbers.append(k)\n\n        # Remove every k-th number from the remaining current_sequence.\n        # This is done by building a new list with elements that are NOT at k-th positions.\n        new_sequence = []\n        for i in range(len(current_sequence)):\n            # Check if the 1-based position of the number is NOT a multiple of k.\n            if (i + 1) % k != 0:\n                new_sequence.append(current_sequence[i])\n        current_sequence = new_sequence\n\n    return ludic_numbers"}
