{"task_id": "Mbpp/603", "solution": "def get_ludic(n: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates Ludic numbers up to n using a sieve method.\n    It returns a list of all Ludic numbers less than or equal to n.\n    \"\"\"\n    numbers = list(range(1, n + 1))\n    ludic_numbers = []\n\n    while numbers:\n        current_ludic = numbers.pop(0)\n        ludic_numbers.append(current_ludic)\n\n        if current_ludic == 1:\n            # Skip sieving when the current Ludic number is 1.\n            continue\n\n        # Sieve numbers: keep only elements whose 1-based index is not a multiple of current_ludic.\n        numbers = [num for i, num in enumerate(numbers) if (i + 1) % current_ludic != 0]\n\n    return ludic_numbers"}
