{"task_id": "Mbpp/608", "solution": "def bell_Number(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Computes the nth Bell number using dynamic programming (Aitken's array).\"\"\"\n    if n == 0:\n        return 1\n\n    # Initialize the first row of Bell's triangle with B_0.\n    bell_row = [1]\n\n    for i in range(1, n + 1):\n        # Create a new row for the triangle.\n        new_row = [0] * (i + 1)\n        # The first element of the new row is the last element of the previous row.\n        new_row[0] = bell_row[-1]\n\n        # Fill the rest of the new row using the recurrence relation.\n        for j in range(1, i + 1):\n            new_row[j] = bell_row[j - 1] + new_row[j - 1]\n\n        # Update bell_row for the next iteration.\n        bell_row = new_row\n\n    # The nth Bell number is the first element of the final row.\n    return bell_row[0]"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/610", "solution": "def remove_kth_element(input_list: list[any], k: int) -> list[any]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Removes the k-th element (1-indexed) from a list, returning a new list.\n    Handles empty lists and out-of-bounds k by returning appropriate copies or empty lists.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not input_list:\n        return []\n\n    if k < 1 or k > len(input_list):\n        return input_list.copy()\n\n    new_list = []\n    # Convert 1-indexed k to 0-indexed position\n    index_to_remove = k - 1\n\n    for i, item in enumerate(input_list):\n        if i != index_to_remove:\n            new_list.append(item)\n\n    return new_list"}
