{"task_id": "Mbpp/622", "solution": "def get_median(list1: list, list2: list, n: int) -> float:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the median of two sorted lists of the same size.\n    It averages the n-th and (n+1)-th elements from the conceptually merged list.\n    \"\"\"\n    i = 0  # Pointer for list1\n    j = 0  # Pointer for list2\n    med1 = 0.0 # Stores the (n)-th smallest element found\n    med2 = 0.0 # Stores the (n+1)-th smallest element found\n\n    # Iterate n+1 times to find the two middle elements of the combined list\n    for _ in range(n + 1):\n        med1 = med2 # Shift med2 to med1, preparing for the next smallest element\n\n        # Determine the next smallest element from either list1 or list2\n        if i == n:\n            # list1 is exhausted, take from list2\n            med2 = float(list2[j])\n            j += 1\n        elif j == n:\n            # list2 is exhausted, take from list1\n            med2 = float(list1[i])\n            i += 1\n        elif list1[i] < list2[j]:\n            # Element in list1 is smaller\n            med2 = float(list1[i])\n            i += 1\n        else:\n            # Element in list2 is smaller or equal\n            med2 = float(list2[j])\n            j += 1\n\n    # The median is the average of the n-th (med1) and (n+1)-th (med2) elements.\n    return (med1 + med2) / 2.0"}
