{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "import math\ndef find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the index of the smallest triangular number that has exactly n digits.\n    This involves finding the smallest k such that T_k >= 10^(n-1).\n    \"\"\"\n    lower_bound = 10**(n - 1)\n    k_float = (-1 + math.sqrt(1 + 8 * lower_bound)) / 2\n    k_index = math.ceil(k_float)\n    return int(k_index)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/740", "solution": "def tuple_to_dict(input_tuple: tuple) -> dict:\n    \"\"\"\n    Converts a tuple into a dictionary using adjacent elements as key-value pairs.\n    The first element of each pair is the key, and the second is the value.\n    \"\"\"\n    result_dict = {}\n    for i in range(0, len(input_tuple) - 1, 2):\n        key = input_tuple[i]\n        value = input_tuple[i + 1]\n        result_dict[key] = value\n    return result_dict"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/739", "solution": "def find_Index(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Calculates the index of the smallest triangular number with 'n' digits.\n    It assumes 'n' is a positive integer.\n    \"\"\"\n    lower_bound_value = 10**(n - 1)\n\n    # Estimate a starting k using the quadratic approximation.\n    k_approx = int((-1 + (1 + 8 * lower_bound_value)**0.5) / 2)\n\n    # Start checking from a safe value around the approximation.\n    k = max(1, k_approx - 2)\n\n    while True:\n        triangular_number = k * (k + 1) // 2\n        # Check if the number meets the lower bound and has exactly 'n' digits.\n        if triangular_number >= lower_bound_value and len(str(triangular_number)) == n:\n            return k\n        k += 1"}
