{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "def _get_digits(num: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"Extracts all individual digits of a number into a list.\n    Example: 123 -> [1, 2, 3].\n    \"\"\"\n    return [int(d) for d in str(num)]\ndef _contains_zero_digit(digits: list[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Checks if the list of digits contains the digit zero.\n    Returns True if zero is found, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    return 0 in digits\ndef _is_divisible_by_all_digits(num: int, digits: list[int]) -> bool:\n    \"\"\"Verifies if the number is perfectly divisible by every digit in its list.\n    Assumes all digits in the list are non-zero.\n    \"\"\"\n    for digit in digits:\n        if num % digit != 0:\n            return False\n    return True\ndef divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within a given range that are divisible by every non-zero digit they contain.\n    Numbers containing the digit zero are excluded.\n    \"\"\"\n    results_list = []\n    for num in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        digits_list = _get_digits(num)\n\n        if not _contains_zero_digit(digits_list):\n            if _is_divisible_by_all_digits(num, digits_list):\n                results_list.append(num)\n\n    return results_list"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/745", "solution": "def divisible_by_digits(startnum: int, endnum: int) -> list[int]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds numbers within a range where each number is divisible by all its digits.\n    Handles the case where a digit is zero by disqualifying the number.\n    \"\"\"\n    result = []\n    for num in range(startnum, endnum + 1):\n        str_num = str(num)\n        is_valid_number = True\n        for digit_char in str_num:\n            digit = int(digit_char)\n            if digit == 0:\n                is_valid_number = False\n                break\n            if num % digit != 0:\n                is_valid_number = False\n                break\n\n        if is_valid_number:\n            result.append(num)\n\n    return result"}
