{"task_id": "Mbpp/765", "solution": "def is_polite(n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the nth polite number, which is a positive integer that is not a power of 2.\n    It iterates through integers, skipping powers of 2, until the nth such number is found.\n    \"\"\"\n    count = 0\n    num = 0\n\n    while True:\n        num += 1\n        # A positive integer is a power of 2 if (num & (num - 1)) == 0.\n        # We check if it's NOT a power of 2 to identify polite numbers.\n        if (num & (num - 1)) != 0:\n            count += 1\n            if count == n:\n                return num"}
