{"task_id": "Mbpp/763", "solution": "def find_min_diff(arr: tuple, n: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Calculates the minimum absolute difference between any two distinct elements in an array.\n    It sorts the array and iterates through adjacent elements to find the smallest difference.\"\"\"\n\n    # Sort the array to efficiently find the minimum difference.\n    sorted_arr = sorted(arr)\n\n    min_diff = float('inf')\n\n    # Iterate through the sorted array to compare adjacent elements.\n    for i in range(n - 1):\n        diff = abs(sorted_arr[i+1] - sorted_arr[i])\n        if diff < min_diff:\n            min_diff = diff\n\n    return int(min_diff)"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/764", "solution": "def number_ctr(input_string: str) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Counts the number of digit characters in the given string.\n    Iterates through the string and increments a counter for each digit found.\n    \"\"\"\n    digit_count = 0\n    for char in input_string:\n        if char.isdigit():\n            digit_count += 1\n    return digit_count"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/766", "solution": "def pair_wise(input_list: list) -> list[tuple]:\n    \"\"\"\n    Generates a list of consecutive pairs from the given input_list.\n    Returns an empty list if input_list has fewer than two elements.\n    \"\"\"\n    if len(input_list) < 2:\n        return []\n\n    result = []\n    for i in range(len(input_list) - 1):\n        result.append((input_list[i], input_list[i+1]))\n    return result"}
