{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "def last(array: list, element: any) -> int:\n    \"\"\"Finds the last position of an element in a sorted array using modified binary search.\n    It assumes the input array is sorted in ascending order.\"\"\"\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n\n        if array[mid] == element:\n            result = mid  # Store this as a potential last occurrence\n            low = mid + 1 # Continue searching in the right half for a later occurrence\n        elif array[mid] < element:\n            low = mid + 1 # Element must be in the right half\n        else: # array[mid] > element\n            high = mid - 1 # Element must be in the left half\n\n    return result"}
