{"task_id": "Mbpp/780", "solution": "import itertools\ndef find_combinations(input_list: list[tuple[int, int]]) -> list[tuple[int, int]]:\n    \"\"\"Calculates element-wise sums of distinct 2-element tuple pairs.\n    Ensures that commutative sums appear only once in the output list.\"\"\"\n    result_sums = []\n    for tuple_a, tuple_b in itertools.combinations(input_list, 2):\n        sum_tuple = (tuple_a[0] + tuple_b[0], tuple_a[1] + tuple_b[1])\n        result_sums.append(sum_tuple)\n    return result_sums"}
{"task_id": "Mbpp/793", "solution": "from typing import List\ndef last(array: List[int], target: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Finds the 0-based index of the last occurrence of the target in a sorted array.\n    Returns -1 if the target is not found or the array is empty.\n    \"\"\"\n    if not array:\n        return -1\n\n    low = 0\n    high = len(array) - 1\n    result = -1\n\n    while low <= high:\n        mid = low + (high - low) // 2\n\n        if array[mid] == target:\n            result = mid\n            low = mid + 1\n        elif array[mid] < target:\n            low = mid + 1\n        else: # array[mid] > target\n            high = mid - 1\n\n    return result"}
