{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number: int, d: int) -> int:\n    \"\"\"\n    Performs a left bit rotation on a 32-bit integer by 'd' positions.\n    Bits wrap around from the most significant end to the least significant end.\n    \"\"\"\n    # Normalize the input number to a 32-bit unsigned integer.\n    number = number & 0xFFFFFFFF\n\n    # Normalize the rotation amount to be within [0, 31].\n    d = d % 32\n\n    # Perform the left shift and right shift for wrap-around, then combine.\n    rotated_value = (number << d) | (number >> (32 - d))\n\n    # Mask the final result to ensure it remains a 32-bit integer.\n    return rotated_value & 0xFFFFFFFF"}
