{"task_id": "Mbpp/803", "solution": "import math\ndef is_perfect_square(number):\n    \"\"\"\n    Determines if a given number is a perfect square.\n    It returns True if the number is a non-negative perfect square, False otherwise.\n    \"\"\"\n    if number < 0:\n        return False\n\n    sqrt_num = math.sqrt(number)\n    # Check if the square root is an integer by comparing it to its integer conversion.\n    # Squaring the integer part and comparing to the original number mitigates float inaccuracies.\n    sqrt_int = int(sqrt_num)\n    return sqrt_int * sqrt_int == number"}
