{"task_id": "Mbpp/799", "solution": "def left_rotate(number, d):\n    BIT_SIZE = 32\n    # Ensure d is within the valid range [0, BIT_SIZE-1]\n    # A rotation by BIT_SIZE bits is equivalent to no rotation.\n    actual_rotation = d % BIT_SIZE\n\n    # Perform the left shift.\n    # Since Python integers have arbitrary precision, we need to mask the result\n    # to keep it within the 32-bit boundary.\n    rotated_part = (number << actual_rotation) & ((1 << BIT_SIZE) - 1)\n\n    # Calculate the bits that wrap around from the left end.\n    wrapped_part = (number >> (BIT_SIZE - actual_rotation))\n\n    # Combine the rotated part and the wrapped-around part using a bitwise OR.\n    return rotated_part | wrapped_part"}
